                    {
                        "header": "Background",
                        "subsections": [
                            {
                                "displayStyle": "row-right",
                                "description": [
                                    "UbuTube (<a href='https://ubu.com' target='_blank'>ubu.com</a>) is a digital avant-garde media library founded in 1996. Notoriously unbound by capital flows, law, or hierarchy, UbuWeb is 'a purposely unstable library, a conflicted curation, an archive assembled by embracing the fragmented, the biased, the subjective, and the incomplete.'[2] ",
                                    "UbuTube's conduct and development over the last thirty years has been admirably reflective of its mission. Its hundreds of thousands of files remain freely and readily accessible to all. However, as anticipated by its creators, some parts of the site have not withstood the test of time. Links are broken, file types are unsupported, and content is scattered all over the place. Given the importance of UbuWeb's work and my particular affinity for avant-garde film, I took to preserving the site through my own guerilla archivism. The result was UbuTube, a hybrid of UbuWeb and YouTube that aims to provide a formal, consistent backdrop for UbuWeb's disparate catalog.",
                                    "UbuTube operates on axioms of minimalism, immediacy, and universality, but also provides its users with a hightened degree of personalization and interactivity. None of the original content has been altered, but the container has been radically changed."                                
                                ],
                                "images": [
                                        
                                    {
                                        "type": "slider",
                                        "srcs": [
                                            {
                                                "src": "/case_studies/ubutube/background_5.png"

                                            },
