                    {
                        "header": "Background",
                        "subsections": [
                            {
                                "displayStyle": "row-right",
                                "description": [
                                    "<a href='https://are.na' target='_blank'>Are.na</a> is a content aggregation website oriented towards artists and designers. The site is based around a hierarchy of 'blocks' and 'channels'. Blocks contain files uploaded by users, while channels are collections of those blocks (and may also contain channels themselves).",
				                    "Since blocks can be shared between channels and appropriated by different users, node connections quickly grow beyond the scope of Are.na's native UI. The relationship between blocks and channels is unidrectional, but the relationship between channels and other channels is bidrectional. With these rules in mind, I created <i>arena flow</i>, a web app that uses <a target='_blank' href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjacency_list'>adjacency lists</a> to dynamically construct directed graphs based on connections between blocks, channels, users, and groups."
                                ],
                                "images": [
                                        
                                    {
                                        "type": "scroll-left",
                                        "srcs": [
                                            {
                                                "src": "/case_studies/arena-flow/background_2.png"
                                            }, 
                                            {
                                                "src": "/case_studies/arena-flow/background_1.png",
                                                "caption": "Representation of Are.na neighborhood associativity. Users [U] create blocks [B] and channels [C]. Channels may contain blocks and other channels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                
                                ]
                            }, 
                            {
                                "displayStyle": "row-left",
                                "description": [
                                    "While Are.na principally acts as a helpful tool for non-technical designers and artists, it also extends a great deal of agency to developers who may wish to extend or modify it. I made full use of the <a href='https://www.are.na/developers/explore' target='_blank'>Are.na developer API</a> to derive and process Are.na's data. The aim was to allow the user to do anything on <i>arena flow</i> that they'd be able to do on Are.na."
                                ],
                                "images": [
                                    {
                                        "type": "scroll-left",
                                        "srcs": [
